{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:ac90a1dbcfb394c03e3af766f7f3fadddd8a08a874b0beff7d1a1a4c1beb458b","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026#R:resp:force","title":"Exponential thresholds and force"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/159a26ec73c0130cf7d4559f.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"r:Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026:R:resp:force","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026","name":"Exponential thresholds and force","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"9.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/responses.tex","label":"R:resp:force","line":22,"manuscript":"Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026","statement_sha256":"66a466d630c3117beb0d18449857472587fe7db586aec052af982b92ff657f32"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026.html#R:resp:force","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":9,"section_title":"Correlation lengths, pulling, and prescribed spatial endpoints","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:d2e90cc56fd30e04d2504a086e0006eb9957626833d6fb254080bd34b193dd7a","file":"preprints/Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/responses.tex","line":22,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"66a466d630c3117beb0d18449857472587fe7db586aec052af982b92ff657f32","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/responses.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d2e90cc56fd30e04d2504a086e0006eb9957626833d6fb254080bd34b193dd7a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Renewal-and-changes-of-law-for-critical-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/responses.tex#L22"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{R:resp:force}\nUniformly over unit vectors $e$, as $t\\downarrow0$,\n\\[\n m_e(t)=t^{3/4+o(1)},\\qquad m_{\\mathrm{rad}}(t)=t^{3/4+o(1)}.\n\\]\nMore precisely, for every $\\varepsilon>0$ and all sufficiently small $t$,\n\\[\n t^{3/4+\\varepsilon}\\le m_{\\mathrm{rad}}(t)\\le m_e(t)\\le C t^{3/4},\n\\]\nwhere $C$ is independent of $e$. For each unit vector $e$ and $s\\ge0$, the limit\n\\[\n f_e(s)=\\lim_{j\\to\\infty}\\frac1j\\log\n \\sum_{\\ell(\\gamma)=j}\\rho^j e^{s e\\cdot(\\gamma_j-o)}\n\\]\nexists. It satisfies $f_e(0)=0$ and\n\\[\n f_e(s)=s^{4/3+o(1)}\\qquad(s\\downarrow0),\n\\]\nuniformly in $e$."}
